<title>USA: Objective IPO trading debut.</title>
<headline>Objective IPO trading debut.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Objective Communications Inc made its trading debut on Thursday, closing at 6-1/2 after the initial public offering priced at $5.50.</p>
<p>The initial public offering of 1.8 million shares of common stock was declared effective on Thursday. The lead underwriter for the deal was Barington Capital Group L.P. Objective Communications granted the underwriter an option to purchase up to 270,000 shares to cover over-allotments.</p>
<p>The company, which trades on the Nasdaq National market under the symbol &quot;OCOM&quot;, is a development stage company.</p>
</text>
